===================================================================================================
  THE PREDICTIONS, SCORED
===================================================================================================
  Q1  B grew 512x (250 -> 128,000); realised distinct values grew 23.94x (17 -> 407)
      ⇒ HELD: the distinct-value count does NOT track B
  Q2  fraction of occupied bins with mean exactly 0.0: 0.9080 at B=250 -> 0.9870 at B=128,000
      ⇒ HELD: it rises with B
  Q3  ⚠️ an EXPLANATION offered for M77's flat-topped ladder, not a demonstration that it
      caused it. A mechanism consistent with a curve is not evidence that it produced it.

===================================================================================================
  HOW TO READ THIS
===================================================================================================
  ⛔ The nominal bin count B is NOT the recalibration's resolution. Quote the realised
     distinct-value count beside any B, or the number overstates what the method can
     express by orders of magnitude.
  ⛔ This is a property of the DATA, not of the method: 99.66% zeros means most bins
     contain no event and therefore all carry the identical forecast 0.0. A different
     binning rule would not repair it; a different target base rate would.
  ⛔ One split, one checkpoint, one seed, sb only, and no σ̂ exists for any of it.

